---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "The Ritz Restaurant",
  servesCuisine: ["British", "Contemporary British"],
  priceRange: "£££££",
  telephone: "+44-20-7300-2370",
  url: "https://www.theritzlondon.com/dine-with-us/the-ritz-restaurant/",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "150 Piccadilly",
    addressLocality: "London",
    postalCode: "W1J 9BR",
    addressCountry: "GB",
  },
  description:
    "The Ritz Restaurant at The Ritz London: two-Michelin-starred dining room in Mayfair serving the Epicurean Journey tasting menus and priced à la carte dishes.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Ritz Restaurant Menu (2026) — Prices, Tasting Menus & Dishes | The Ritz Menu Guide"
  description="Independent guide to The Ritz Restaurant's menu: Epicurean Journey 5-course £215 and 7-course £235, weekday three-course lunch £105, à la carte dishes with official prices, Arts de la Table, hours, and the two Michelin stars."
  path="/the-ritz-restaurant-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/ritz-restaurant.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/ritz-restaurant.webp"
      alt="Illustration of an elegant fine-dining table with silver cloche and crystal glasses (illustrative artwork, not the actual Ritz)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · The Ritz London · Mayfair
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      The Ritz Restaurant — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The Ritz Restaurant is the grand dining room of The Ritz London at 150 Piccadilly —
      a two-Michelin-starred room (promoted in the 2025 Guide) that was named
      <strong>Restaurant of the Year</strong> by the National Restaurant Awards 2025.
      Executive Chef John Williams MBE, in the kitchen since 2004, cooks contemporary
      British food built on classic Escoffier technique. This guide summarises the menus
      and prices from <strong>official Ritz sources</strong> (the September 2026 tasting
      and lunch menu PDFs and the August 2025 à la carte menu) in our own
      words — with the official PDFs linked below so you can read the full text yourself.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">150 Piccadilly, London W1J 9BR — The Ritz London</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">John Williams MBE, Executive Chef since 2004</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Awards</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Two Michelin stars (2025 Guide); National Restaurant Awards 2025 — Restaurant of the Year</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Lunch</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Daily 12:30 PM – 2:00 PM</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Dinner</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Daily 6:30 PM – 9:00 PM</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Phone</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">+44 (0) 20 7300 2370 (official site, October 2026)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>The Epicurean Journey (tasting menus)</h2>
      <p>
        The signature experience is the Epicurean Journey — a tasting menu built around
        "the love and knowledge of gourmet food and fine wine," available before
        <strong>1:45 PM at lunch and 8:45 PM at dinner</strong> (official Epicurean
        Journey sample menu, September 2026).
        Two lengths:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Five-course experience — £215 per person.</strong> Optional five-glass wine pairing: Classic £125, Fine £235, Prestige £725.</li>
        <li><strong>Seven-course experience — £235 per person.</strong> Optional six-glass wine pairing: Classic £150, Fine £280, Prestige £870.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All prices include VAT; a discretionary <strong>12.5% service charge</strong> is added
        to the bill (official menus, September 2026). On Friday and Saturday evenings, choosing
        the à la carte or Epicurean menus also carries a <strong>£58 per person
        entertainment charge</strong> (live entertainment on those nights — official
        restaurant page, October 2026).
      </p>

      <h2>Lunch at The Ritz Restaurant</h2>
      <p>
        Lunch is served <strong>daily, 12:30 PM – 2:00 PM</strong> (official restaurant
        page, October 2026), and it is the best-value way into the room — the £58
        Friday/Saturday entertainment charge applies to <strong>evenings only</strong>,
        never at lunch.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Weekday three-course lunch — £105 per person</strong> (official three-course sample lunch menu, September 2026). Served at <strong>lunchtime Monday to Friday only</strong>; a supplement course is £16 and an additional course £33.</li>
        <li><strong>Epicurean Journey at lunch</strong> — the five-course (£215) and seven-course (£235) tasting menus are both available at lunch; they must be ordered <strong>before 1:45 PM</strong> (official Epicurean Journey sample menu, September 2026).</li>
        <li><strong>À la carte at lunch</strong> — the same dishes and prices as dinner; the Ritz publishes no separate lunch pricing for à la carte.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Two house rules worth knowing: a <strong>minimum spend of two courses per
        guest</strong> applies (official menus page), and the dress code —
        <strong>jacket and tie for gentlemen</strong> — is enforced at lunch exactly as
        at dinner. All lunch prices include VAT; the discretionary 12.5% service charge
        is added to the bill.
      </p>

      <h2>À la carte — first courses</h2>
      <p>
        Sample starters from the official August 2025 menu (described in our own words):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dorset crab (£50)</strong> — with crème fraîche and imperial caviar.</li>
        <li><strong>Langoustine (£55)</strong> — à la nage with bronze fennel.</li>
        <li><strong>Ballotine of duck liver (£42)</strong> — with cherry and pistachio.</li>
        <li><strong>Roast quail (£45)</strong> — with hazelnut and verjus.</li>
        <li><strong>Pea velouté (£40)</strong> — with smoked bacon and pecorino.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>À la carte — main courses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Wild sea bass (£64)</strong> — with saffron and Menton lemon.</li>
        <li><strong>Cornish turbot "Ton sur Ton" (£85)</strong> — the priciest main on the menu.</li>
        <li><strong>Suffolk lamb (£65)</strong> — with Roscoff onion and mint.</li>
        <li><strong>Brittany pigeon (£65)</strong> — with apricot and smoked almond.</li>
        <li><strong>Fillet of veal (£68)</strong> — with English pea and lovage.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Arts de la Table — tableside classics</h2>
      <p>
        A Ritz signature: dishes finished or served at the table ("the timeless dining
        tradition of table side service"). These <strong>serve two guests</strong> and need
        about <strong>40 minutes' preparation</strong> (official menu, August 2025):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Dover sole (£170)</strong> — "sentiments of the sea," for two.</li>
        <li><strong>Beef Wellington (£150)</strong> — with hen of the wood mushrooms and Périgord truffle, for two.</li>
        <li><strong>Crêpe Suzette (£65)</strong> — for two; the legendary flambéed dessert created by Henri Carpentier in 1895, prepared tableside.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A <strong>selection of artisan cheeses from the trolley</strong> is £33.
      </p>

      <h2>Desserts</h2>
      <p>
        All listed desserts are <strong>£27</strong> in the official August 2025 menu —
        the Ritz chocolate soufflé with vanilla chantilly, the Ritz signature chocolate
        with hazelnut and fudge, a vanilla–almond praline dessert with Dulcey and banana
        ice cream, rum-soaked baba with exotic fruits and vanilla, and English strawberry
        with lemon verbena and lime.
      </p>

      <h2>Champagne &amp; wine</h2>
      <p>
        The menu lists a "Champagne of the month" — at the time of the August 2025 menu,
        a Taittinger selection: Brut Réserve NV £28 (glass, 150ml) / £130 (bottle),
        Prestige Rosé NV £32 / £150, Vintage Brut 2016 £38 / £175, Comtes de Champagne
        2013 £78 / £365, and Comtes de Champagne Rosé 2011 at £640. Champagne selections
        rotate, so check the current menu.
      </p>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one visit, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>The full occasion:</strong> the five-course Epicurean Journey at £215 — it's the menu the room is built around, and only £20 less than the seven-course.</li>
        <li><strong>À la carte pick:</strong> the langoustine à la nage (£55) to start, the turbot (£85) for main — the two dishes the kitchen is most associated with.</li>
        <li><strong>The theatre:</strong> the tableside crêpe Suzette (£65 for two) — it's a piece of dining history, and you can't get this performance many places.</li>
        <li><strong>Watch the extras:</strong> Friday/Saturday adds £58pp entertainment on top of menu prices, before the 12.5% service charge. See our <a href="/ritz-menu-prices/">price guide</a> for realistic totals.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book well ahead:</strong> see our <a href="/ritz-booking-guide/">booking guide</a> for how far ahead to reserve and the dress code (jacket and tie for gentlemen).</li>
        <li><strong>Breakfast is for residents first:</strong> the restaurant serves breakfast 7:30–10:30 AM for hotel residents, 7:30–10:00 AM for non-residents.</li>
        <li><strong>Dietary needs:</strong> allergen, vegan and vegetarian menus are available — tell the team when booking, per the official menu.</li>
        <li><strong>The room:</strong> lunch and dinner are served beneath the restaurant's soaring glass roof — widely considered one of the most beautiful dining rooms in London.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/dine-with-us/the-ritz-restaurant/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — theritzlondon.com</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/content/uploads/2026/09/Epicurean-Journey-Sample-Menu-09.26.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official Epicurean Journey menu (PDF, September 2026) — tasting menu prices</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/content/uploads/2026/09/3-Course-Sample-Menu-09.26.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official three-course lunch menu (PDF, September 2026) — weekday lunch prices</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/content/uploads/2025/08/ALC-Menu-040825.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official à la carte menu (PDF, August 2025) — full priced menu</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.theritzlondon.com/press-release/the-ritz-restaurant-awarded-two-michelin-stars/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Two Michelin stars — Ritz announcement (Feb 2025)</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        All prices above come from <strong>official Ritz sources</strong>: the Epicurean
        Journey and three-course lunch menus (PDFs, September 2026) and the à la carte
        menu (PDF, August 2025), checked October 2026. Prices include VAT; a
        discretionary 12.5% service charge is added to the bill. Menus and prices change
        with the seasons —
        always verify with the hotel before visiting. Descriptions are our own summaries;
        the official PDFs linked above carry the full menu text.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Ritz guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/ritz-menu-prices/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Menu prices — what dinner really costs</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— realistic totals with service charge</span></li>
        <li><a href="/ritz-afternoon-tea/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Afternoon tea at the Palm Court</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— from £95 per adult</span></li>
        <li><a href="/ritz-booking-guide/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">How to book</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— reservations, dress code, tips</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
